          ],
          "cookies": [],
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "size": 30948,
            "text": "{\"records\":[{\"sha\":\"ba60e5d588e7a5935198bf76c5b373020d08d2d3\",\"parents\":[\"355d14a98da3104e31aa39e52bf1469726a80933\"],\"message\":\"chore(evals): approve the hello-mcp case (#20)\\n\\nThe case was proposed as a draft, so recipe-check reported\\npi.evals_case_unapproved; approving it leaves the Recipe with no diagnostics.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XR2prBe3MguZKEdga8mtt7\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-11-05T23:16:34+11:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-11-05T23:16:34+11:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"355d14a98da3104e31aa39e52bf1469726a80933\",\"parents\":[\"f12cffb97ee8e0416f18570ff57f02e13beb6dbf\"],\"message\":\"feat(evals): the Harbor task names its case hello-mcp, with its case file (#19)\\n\\nMove the task from harbor/ to evals/harbor/hello-mcp/, the Recipe format's\\ndefault layout, so its folder name is its case id. Name the case in\\n`[metadata] case` too, add the draft case file evals/cases/hello-mcp.md, and\\nopt into the eval layout checks with `pi.evals: {}`. A new .recipeignore keeps\\nevals/ out of deployed runtimes, which the format requires once pi.evals is\\ndeclared. Scripts and docs follow the new task path.\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Marcus Schiesser\",\"email\":\"marcus.schiesser@googlemail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-11-05T09:17:28+01:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-11-05T09:17:28+01:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"f12cffb97ee8e0416f18570ff57f02e13beb6dbf\",\"parents\":[\"c77869250658d76a185813ac186914c14dccbc7e\"],\"message\":\"fix: drop environment/Dockerfile for docker_image so the task runs on a plane, and move the agent to Sonnet 5.5 (#17)\\n\\nProblem: the Introspection Harbor adapter refuses a task whose\\nenvironment/Dockerfile nothing on a plane builds (unused_dockerfile),\\nbecause the Runtime image fills main there; deleting the file alone\\nleaves Harbor's local Docker provider composing main from it.\\n\\nObjective: main's task must run as a kind: eval trial on a plane, and\\nthe local Docker trial must still get an agent container, now from\\ntask.toml's docker_image (buildpack-deps:noble-curl: Ubuntu 24.04 with\\nca-certificates and curl, what the Dockerfile built). The agent moves\\nfrom claude-sonnet-4-6 to claude-sonnet-5-5.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XR2prAhtGPTsPw6GEqGRFZ\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"cyharyanto@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-11-02T14:13:09+11:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-11-02T14:13:09+11:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"c77869250658d76a185813ac186914c14dccbc7e\",\"parents\":[\"543b8db50a839029b03d7ca7957884d806df646c\"],\"message\":\"refactor: bind hello-mcp from task.toml and fix the eval run invocation (#15)\\n\\n* fix: commit a loopback hello-mcp binding for platform eval trials\\n\\nA platform eval trial reads the Recipe's committed .pi/mcp.local.json, so the\\nsidecar world needs the file in the checkout. Recipe validation accepts a\\ncommitted binding only to a loopback URL, so it names localhost:8000, which\\nreaches the sidecar through the pod's shared network namespace.\\n\\nrun-local.sh swaps the compose-name binding in for a local Docker trial, where\\nmcp-server is a separate container, and restores the committed file on exit.\\ndocs/mcp-bindings.md explains how the id is bound in each world.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* chore: align .gitignore with the recipe template\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* chore: remove the token-bearing remote MCP binding example\\n\\nA credential-bearing binding belongs outside the repository; run-local.sh\\ntakes its path through HELLO_MCP_BINDING.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* docs: call out task.toml's mcp_servers declaration and its status\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* Revert \\\"chore: remove the token-bearing remote MCP binding example\\\"\\n\\nThis reverts commit 950c834a66c5fa979fd57c4d098d3e5d9f0d5c81.\\n\\n* docs: document the remote example as a run-local.sh binding\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* refactor: simplify run-local.sh and document both local runs\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* fix: pass --path and --runtime to introspection eval run\\n\\nCLI 0.60 rejects a positional task path, and two Runtime manifests share this\\ndirectory, so a run must name one.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* refactor: bind hello-mcp from task.toml through the Harbor adapter\\n\\nThe Introspection Harbor adapter writes a task's [[environment.mcp_servers]]\\ninto the Recipe's .pi/mcp.local.json on every run, local and platform, so the\\ncommitted loopback binding and run-local.sh's copy were redundant. Drop both\\nand the sidecar example, ignore .pi/mcp.local.json again, and document the\\nrule: name is the Recipe's MCP id, the URL host is the compose service name.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n* docs: add a localhost example binding for introspection local\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MSyVHjjitFHSH9wrHgaesL\\n\\n---------\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-28T15:17:43-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-10-28T15:17:43-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"543b8db50a839029b03d7ca7957884d806df646c\",\"parents\":[\"e3327a0d0d127aa0c8e690fce48e292caf28b86f\"],\"message\":\"chore: introspection check as npm scripts and a pre-commit hook (#14)\\n\\nThe same check the travel-agent recipe runs: `npm run check`, and a\\npre-commit hook wired by `prepare` (core.hooksPath .githooks).\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-23T11:54:19-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-10-23T11:54:19-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"e3327a0d0d127aa0c8e690fce48e292caf28b86f\",\"parents\":[\"dab077fe149ee1d1776fdbf8638e1c4d6d5dc8ee\"],\"message\":\"feat: add a scripted agent on the platform's model double for the SDK end-to-end walk (#13)\\n\\n* feat: add a scripted agent on the platform's model double for the SDK end-to-end walk\\n\\nSame tools, MCP opt-in and instructions as agents/agent.yaml, on\\nintrospection/scripted-llm, selected per task with agent_name.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* fix: the scripted agent's thinking level is one the validator accepts\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-23T11:10:37-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-10-23T11:10:37-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"dab077fe149ee1d1776fdbf8638e1c4d6d5dc8ee\",\"parents\":[\"e6dce0f7a9ecd20b19dea1dd6a1b2c1836693d2e\"],\"message\":\"chore: declare the model under `ai`, matching template-starter (#12)\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-20T12:15:12-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-20T12:15:12-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"e6dce0f7a9ecd20b19dea1dd6a1b2c1836693d2e\",\"parents\":[\"25e48d70141b968462bd39d6e18747e051b00e54\"],\"message\":\"feat: run the hello-mcp task against a compose sidecar or the remote connector (#11)\\n\\n* feat: run the hello-mcp task against a compose sidecar or the remote connector\\n\\nThe task keeps Harbor's contract verbatim and gains its world as a compose\\nfile: `main` is the agent slot and `mcp-server` is the hello MCP, built from\\nmcp/ for a local Docker trial and published as an image for the platform,\\nwhere it runs as a sidecar of the trial's sandbox pod. `.pi/mcp.local.json`\\nbinds the Recipe's `hello-mcp` id to `http://mcp-server:8000/mcp`, which\\nresolves in both places; a Runtime with the hello-mcp connector bound\\nresolves the same id to the public server instead, so one Recipe, one\\ninstruction and one judge serve both worlds.\\n\\nscripts/run-task.sh creates the trial as a non-interactive `kind: eval` task\\ntagged `harbor`, sending the compose document as the task's `compose` field\\nfor the sidecar world and going through `introspection tasks create` for the\\nremote one. judges/greeting.yaml is tests/test.sh over the trajectory.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9nE5Bydq14tspyNHNjMrF\\n\\n* fix: ship the sidecar MCP binding as an example, not a committed local config\\n\\nrecipes check refuses a committed .pi/mcp.local.json (local capability\\nconfiguration must not be distributed with a Recipe), so the sidecar binding\\nis .pi/mcp.sidecar.example.json, copied into place for a local run. Carrying\\nthe same binding to the sandbox with the task is the follow-up.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9nE5Bydq14tspyNHNjMrF\\n\\n* fix: build the sidecar image through the images API before the task\\n\\nThe sidecar world stripped `build:` and passed `image: ghcr.io/…:0.1.0`\\nstraight through, on the stated assumption that a sidecar is pulled and\\nnever built. That stopped being true. A compose service must now name a\\nready image of the caller's project (introspection-cloud#2631,\\n`ImageService.resolve_compose`, `compose_images_require_catalog` on by\\ndefault), so the create 422s on an unmirrored tag — and a mirror has to be\\ndigest-pinned, which `:0.1.0` is not.\\n\\nEach sidecar's `build:` context is now packed, uploaded through the Files\\nAPI and built through `POST /v1/images`, and the digest-pinned reference\\nthe row returns replaces the build/image pair. That is the same path\\n`IntrospectionEnvironment.resolve_images()` takes in the CLI adapter, and\\nit drops the ghcr dependency: `mcp/Dockerfile` becomes the single source\\nrather than a published tag that has to be kept in step.\\n\\nThe two compose transforms move into `scripts/compose_builds.py` and\\n`scripts/compose_resolved.py` — the second heredoc could not nest inside\\nthe first, and both are easier to run on their own this way.\\n\\nAlso records what the sidecar world now needs of its credential: `kind:\\neval` requires `tasks:eval` and the image create requires `images:write`,\\nso the token must be an API key carrying the `evals` capability.\\n\\n`pull_reference` is a plain property the API does not serialize, so the\\nscript composes `image_ref@image_digest` itself.\\n\\nValidated: both helpers run against the task's real compose file, and the\\ndocument they produce validates against the platform's own `TaskCompose`\\nmodel — one sidecar, healthcheck preserved, port 8000, `main` carrying\\nonly `depends_on`.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9nE5Bydq14tspyNHNjMrF\\n\\n* feat: deploy the Runtime from its own script, and stop run-e2b brokering\\n\\nThree changes that together make the four shapes runnable in order.\\n\\n`deploy-runtime.sh` is new, and it is the step every other script assumed\\nhad already happened without any of them doing it: run-e2b.sh reads the\\nversion's published E2B template out of image_build_metadata, and\\nrun-task.sh names the Runtime by slug and lets the Data Plane resolve the\\nlatest ready version. Neither creates one. It takes `--manifest` because\\nthat is what picks the world — hello-mcp-local.yaml has no connector and\\nserves the sidecar world, hello-mcp.yaml carries the binding — waits on\\nimage_build_status, and prints the id on stdout so a caller can capture it.\\n\\n`run-e2b.sh` no longer touches the connector. It was resolving a\\nconnection, brokering a token and, failing that, running an interactive\\nconsent flow inline — all of which setup-introspection.sh already does and\\nowns. What is left resolves the template and runs. Under managed egress\\nnothing travels at all now: the proxy injects both the model key and the\\nRuntime's own hello-mcp credential, where the old passthrough always sent\\na token it had just brokered. An explicit HELLO_MCP_TOKEN still wins, for\\na direct run against the public server, and a run with neither says which\\nof the two to set rather than opening a browser.\\n\\nThe README gains the four shapes as one table, the order of operations,\\nand why an E2B trial cannot take the sidecar world: only the in-cluster\\nproviders render a second container, and E2B has no pod, so there is no\\nshared network namespace to put compose services on loopback.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9nE5Bydq14tspyNHNjMrF\\n\\n* fix: create the eval task against the Data Plane, with a resolved runtime id\\n\\nFour things stopped this script running at all.\\n\\n`POST /v1/tasks` takes `runtime_id`, a concrete Runtime version, and forbids\\nunknown fields — so the sidecar world's `runtime: \\\"<slug>\\\"` was a guaranteed\\n422. The slug is now resolved through the Control Plane the way run-e2b.sh\\nresolves it, and both worlds send the id.\\n\\nThe remote world called `introspection tasks create --kind eval`, and no such\\nflag exists: that command posts to the Control Plane's runtime-run route, which\\nmints a runner and cannot say `kind: eval`. A login could not create a trial\\nanyway — the capability it carries has no `evals`. So both worlds now create\\nthe task directly against the Data Plane with the orchestrator's key, which is\\nthe only credential that could ever have worked.\\n\\n`INTROSPECTION_API_BASE_URL` is the CLI's *Control Plane* variable, and the\\nscript used it as the Data Plane base — so the `runtimes list` above would have\\nbeen sent to the sandbox API. The Data Plane is `INTROSPECTION_DP_URL`, which\\nthe CLI already reads for exactly this.\\n\\nFinally the header asked for \\\"an evals-capability API key\\\", which cannot upload\\nthe instruction or a build context: `files:write` lives in the `runtimes`\\nbundle, and the evals bundle's own comment says it is granted beside it. The\\nkey needs both.\\n\\n* refactor: lay the task out the way Harbor lays out its own examples\\n\\nharbor/examples/tasks/hello-mcp/environment holds the Dockerfile, the compose\\nfile and the server it builds side by side. This repo had the task under\\n`harbor-task/` and the MCP server at the repository root, so the compose\\ncontext was `../../mcp` — reaching outside the task directory, which is the\\none thing a Harbor task should never need to do to describe its own world.\\n\\nThe server moves to `environment/mcp-server/` and the context becomes\\n`./mcp-server`, so the task is self-contained and reads like the upstream\\nexample it mirrors.\\n\\nAlso drops the `image:` that sat beside `build:`. It named\\nghcr.io/introspection-org/recipe-harbor-mcp-agent/mcp-server:0.1.0, which\\nnothing publishes, so `docker compose pull` would fail and a reader would take\\nit for an authoritative source. The build context is the only source: a local\\ntrial builds it, and the platform substitutes what that same context produced\\nthrough POST /v1/images, since a sidecar is pulled and never built.\\n\\n* docs: keep the published image as a commented alternative to building\\n\\nDeleting it lost the fact that pulling a published server is a supported shape,\\nnot just an unfinished one. It stays commented beside the build context with\\nthe swap spelled out, so the file shows both sources while naming only one.\\n\\n* refactor: put the Harbor task under harbor/\\n\\nNothing in the toolchain constrains this name: the CLI detects a Harbor\\nevaluation by finding `task.toml` at the path it is given (or within four\\nlevels of it), so `--path` always names the directory and no convention is\\nenforced. What does exist is the platform's own vocabulary — the Data Plane\\nreads the task's location from `metadata.harbor.task` when it resolves a\\ncompose service by name against the image catalog — so naming the directory\\nfor the tool it configures matches the one place the platform already spells\\nit, rather than inventing a second convention beside it.\\n\\nNaming it for the task instead put a task name at the root of a Recipe, beside\\n`agents/` and `judges/`, which reads as though the Recipe were the task. A\\nsecond task would live at `harbor/<name>/`; `metadata.harbor.task` carries\\nwhichever shape without changing.\\n\\n* feat: add run-local.sh, and mark run-task.sh as interim\\n\\nHarbor's own Docker provider is the shape that verifies the task rather than\\nthe platform: compose brings up `main` and `mcp-server`, the verifier reads the\\nresult, and nothing uploads an image or needs a plane. It was two documented\\ncommands with a third, easily forgotten step in front — copying the git-ignored\\n`.pi/mcp.local.json` binding into place, without which the required `hello-mcp`\\nid resolves to nothing. That is now one script.\\n\\n`run-task.sh` earns its place only until introspection-cli#368 lands.\\nIt uploads each build context, polls `/v1/images`, substitutes the digest and\\nposts the task by hand because the CLI could not yet do any of it;\\n`IntrospectionEnvironment` does the same sequence in code, so the two platform\\nrows collapse into `introspection eval run` against that environment with no\\nscript of ours in the middle. Said so in the README rather than leaving a\\nreader to wonder which path is the real one.\\n\\n* refactor: drop run-task.sh in favour of the Harbor environment\\n\\nThe script uploaded each build context, polled /v1/images, substituted the\\ndigest-pinned reference and posted the `kind: eval` task by hand, because the\\nCLI could not yet do any of it. `IntrospectionEnvironment` now runs that exact\\nsequence in code — read the compose file, resolve every sidecar through the\\nimages API, build the task body — so keeping the shell version means two\\nimplementations of one contract, only one of which is maintained or tested.\\n\\nIts two compose helpers go with it: `compose_builds.py` and\\n`compose_resolved.py` existed solely to give the script what\\n`sidecar_services`, `build_context` and `translate_compose` give the adapter.\\n\\n`run-local.sh` and `run-e2b.sh` stay: the first verifies the task on Harbor's\\nown Docker provider with no plane involved, and the second is the one shape\\nHarbor drives without the plane creating the sandbox.\\n\\n* feat: add run-eval-compose.sh, the whole platform contract in one run\\n\\nExercises what a Harbor trial does, with curl and the CLI: build this task's\\nown compose `build.context` through the Files API and POST /v1/images, create a\\n`kind: eval` task carrying the digest-pinned result as a compose service, wait\\nfor the sandbox, then run one command *inside* the sidecar and one *from the\\nagent* reaching it by compose name. A pass means the image catalog, the compose\\ngate, the sidecar rendering and the commands surface all agree.\\n\\n`--mirror <ref@sha256:...>` runs the same trial with the image copied from a\\nremote registry instead of built, which is the catalog's other source and the\\nsame row, gate and reference at the end of it.\\n\\nThe reachability check is deliberately not \\\"2xx\\\": this server answers 404 at\\n`/` and a plain file server answers 200, so the status code says nothing about\\nwhether the hop worked. What it refuses is a gateway 5xx or no response at all\\n— the first is the egress proxy answering for a name it cannot route, which is\\nexactly what a missing NO_PROXY entry looks like from inside the sandbox, and\\nthe second is never having reached anything.\\n\\n* docs: correct the capability the sidecar world needs, and name the fifth run shape\\n\\nThree things the README said were no longer true of the tree:\\n\\n- The sidecar world was documented as needing the `evals` capability alone.\\n  It needs `runtimes` as well: uploading the image's build context goes\\n  through the Files API, and `files:write` is in RUNTIMES_CAPABILITY_SCOPES,\\n  not EVALS_CAPABILITY_SCOPES. An evals-only key reaches the upload and\\n  fails there, which is a confusing place to discover it.\\n- `run-eval-compose.sh` was not in the table of run shapes, so the only way\\n  to exercise the whole contract was undiscoverable from the README.\\n- The `--compose` flag note pointed at introspection-cli#350, which\\n  IntrospectionEnvironment supersedes; and \\\"the script prints 1 or 0\\\"\\n  outlived the run-task.sh it referred to.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P9nE5Bydq14tspyNHNjMrF\\n\\n* feat: run-introspection.sh — the platform contract against any plane\\n\\nRenamed from run-eval-compose.sh and widened, because what it tests is the\\nIntrospection side of a trial rather than the compose piece alone: build the\\ntask's own context through the Files and images APIs, scan it, create a\\n`kind: eval` task carrying the digest-pinned result as a compose service, wait\\nfor the sandbox, then drive it through POST /v1/tasks/{id}/commands.\\n\\nNothing is read off this machine, so the same run works against a local stack,\\nstaging or production — point INTROSPECTION_DP_URL at the plane and give it a\\nkey for that project. It defaults to localhost because that is where it is\\ncheapest to be wrong.\\n\\nNow covers the transfer commands, which nothing did: an upload, a read-back\\nfrom inside the sandbox, and a download, comparing bytes rather than statuses —\\na transfer that reports success and truncates is the failure worth catching. It\\nfound one immediately: the Docker provider's upload still dialled an HTTP file\\nAPI no image serves, and answered 404.\\n\\nTransfer files upload with `encryption: false` and are deleted on exit, the way\\nthe Harbor adapter does it: they exist to cross into the sandbox, app-level\\nencryption costs time and buys nothing, and a large build context exceeds its\\nlimits anyway.\\n\\n`--mirror` runs the same trial from an image copied out of a remote registry,\\nwhich is the catalog's other source.\\n\\n---------\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-07T11:05:55-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-07T11:05:55-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"25e48d70141b968462bd39d6e18747e051b00e54\",\"parents\":[\"bbe73d9b6288d14f4ec678c934e25fd8906b4f7c\"],\"message\":\"chore: trigger a rebuild\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-04T16:43:10-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-04T16:44:00-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"bbe73d9b6288d14f4ec678c934e25fd8906b4f7c\",\"parents\":[\"7b14685faf174e8c686ac9c58837d925f9f3c7c4\"],\"message\":\"feat: declare the hello-mcp connector requirement and validate the Recipe in CI (#9)\\n\\n* feat: declare the hello-mcp connector requirement in the manifest\\n\\n`runtime.connectors: [hello-mcp]` records on every deployed runtime version\\nthat this Recipe needs the `hello-mcp` connector backing its `hello-mcp` MCP\\nserver, so the Runtime page can offer Connect with the connector, connection\\nand MCP binding resolved instead of a bare endpoint form. The README explains\\nthe console path beside the existing CLI setup.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VJ9YQtGgCehDz6jZ3MDP79\\n\\n* ci: validate the Recipe on pull requests and main\\n\\nThe same `recipe validation` workflow recipe-coding-agent runs\\n(`introspection-org/recipes-action@v0`), so `introspection check` gates\\nevery change — including the new `runtime.connectors` declaration once\\nthe CLI release that validates it ships.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VJ9YQtGgCehDz6jZ3MDP79\\n\\n---------\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-04T13:17:06-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-04T13:17:06-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"7b14685faf174e8c686ac9c58837d925f9f3c7c4\",\"parents\":[\"df6a833dd37d6f915d4a93057800031cdd432930\"],\"message\":\"fix(harbor): write greeting to writable temp path (#8)\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-04T10:19:51-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-04T10:19:51-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"df6a833dd37d6f915d4a93057800031cdd432930\",\"parents\":[\"db0325e9385c12cdb7ab998f2f3568f60f97b789\"],\"message\":\"fix: assign hello MCP connection to runtime (#3)\\n\\n* fix: assign hello MCP connection to runtime\\n\\n* chore: retry hello MCP E2B build\\n\\n* docs: separate managed and direct E2B runs\\n\\n* docs: lead with direct E2B workflow\\n\\n* docs: remove obsolete Harbor sync mode\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T15:35:25-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-03T15:35:25-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"db0325e9385c12cdb7ab998f2f3568f60f97b789\",\"parents\":[\"ea4a7c13dad1e7be8e47ad0083356292651cdff8\"],\"message\":\"fix: preserve managed egress credentials in E2B (#6)\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T12:18:19-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-03T12:18:19-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"ea4a7c13dad1e7be8e47ad0083356292651cdff8\",\"parents\":[\"eaccb950d697c7fb5b2afe885f227e0d095d2c2b\"],\"message\":\"fix: bind setup authorization to runtime (#5)\\n\\n* fix: bind setup authorization to runtime\\n\\n* chore: retrigger E2B preview build\\n\\n* fix: verify MCP authorization before evaluation\\n\\n* chore: retry bake with refreshed MCP authorization\\n\\n* chore: retry bake after verified authorization\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T10:21:23-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-03T10:21:23-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"eaccb950d697c7fb5b2afe885f227e0d095d2c2b\",\"parents\":[\"d2dc624587e2d73c5b00e34707d5bf3436d74df6\",\"c0789ba7be498f04c97125d08e3ce8ae70993f2c\"],\"message\":\"Merge pull request #2 from introspection-org/fix/resolve-e2b-runtime-artifact\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T15:16:01-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-02T15:16:01-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"c0789ba7be498f04c97125d08e3ce8ae70993f2c\",\"parents\":[\"c41a612446c0067b745297ac9a3a0ff85aaefad9\"],\"message\":\"docs: record native Pi prompt-file evaluation path\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T14:20:17-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-02T14:20:17-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"c41a612446c0067b745297ac9a3a0ff85aaefad9\",\"parents\":[\"f388998df9b5460385dd3e7bd6299ca0b8998512\"],\"message\":\"chore: retry hello MCP runtime build\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:45:30-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:45:30-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"f388998df9b5460385dd3e7bd6299ca0b8998512\",\"parents\":[\"82f28d4603404b17c08605fbe987635a8fe296e2\"],\"message\":\"fix: confirm non-interactive runtime bootstrap\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:43:29-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:43:29-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"82f28d4603404b17c08605fbe987635a8fe296e2\",\"parents\":[\"2437964323cca29979637f177e9447897e254802\"],\"message\":\"fix: make clean setup repeatable\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:40:53-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:40:53-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"2437964323cca29979637f177e9447897e254802\",\"parents\":[\"4f5676c87bd25cf9d1ad7007c528b22c7a0586e8\"],\"message\":\"feat: add clean Introspection setup workflow\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:38:28-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:38:28-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"4f5676c87bd25cf9d1ad7007c528b22c7a0586e8\",\"parents\":[\"d2dc624587e2d73c5b00e34707d5bf3436d74df6\"],\"message\":\"fix: resolve E2B alias from runtime metadata\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:19:07-07:00\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":null,\"date\":\"2026-09-02T11:19:07-07:00\"}},{\"sha\":\"d2dc624587e2d73c5b00e34707d5bf3436d74df6\",\"parents\":[\"76e22f182a958b5697532d4391e9f2f085ec1f2b\",\"2b0d714af68ad69fbacd9dabd4d080c393b85ad9\"],\"message\":\"Merge pull request #1 from intro